  "description": "Reads a DeepSharp pipeline's rows out of Microsoft's DataFrame, Microsoft.Data.Analysis, or out of anything that can fill one: a comma-separated file, a database query, rows somebody already had. One reader for the long tail of formats, so the pipeline itself needs none of them. A comma-separated file comes through as the text it writes, so the pipeline's own schema decides what each column holds, and a database query says what its columns hold as the database types them. An absent value stays absent rather than becoming a not-a-number, because never-there and arithmetic-went-wrong are different answers.",
